Corresponding Source (AGPL-3.0 section 6)
-----------------------------------------

The Corresponding Source of a Mnemos release is the git commit it was built
from, published at the repository named in script/source-url, plus the
source archive published next to its installers (that commit's tree and the
vendored source of every Rust dependency). The About page of the app and the
copy of this NOTICE inside each installer name that commit and link to it.
The release scripts refuse to build from a tree with uncommitted or untracked
changes, or from a commit that is not on that public repository, so a release
is exactly its commit.

Some Rust dependencies are forks fetched from git repositories that Warp
hosts (the `git = "https://github.com/warpdotdev/..."` entries in the
Cargo.toml files), and a few of them follow a branch. Cargo.lock pins the
exact revision of each, and the release source archive contains it. For those
dependencies the source archive, not the git repository, is the canonical
source of a release.


